harrow reads cairn's files directly rather than shelling out, which makes it a
second implementation of somebody else's format. A second implementation held
only to its own author's reading of the specification is a rumour about the
specification. This is the corpus the reference implementation holds itself to.

`format-N/` holds items as that format wrote them, with the values they parsed
to then. Those directories are frozen by definition: an implementation that
intends to read what people have already written has to keep reading them.

Editing an expectation here is not a fix. It means claiming the format changed,
which needs a format number and a migration — take it up with cairn.
